      "gap": "Aligned and opposite-history simultaneous I/Q with one compensated reference pair complete selected frames, but aligned decision spans0.92837--1.05964V and motion9.69mV/150ps remain inaccurate despite stable codes. Observation-only probes reveal high-reference tail below its reported saturation boundary in all24 decision windows. Input-width and independent diode-biased tail DC experiments improve headroom without qualifying regulation; no candidate adopted. Ideal targets/bias/compensation, startup/noise/mismatch, skew and shared supplies remain missing or unqualified. Later scoped terminal-current replay shows pulsed CDAC demand and reservoir withdrawal; worst high-reference decision error remains about61mV. Doubling high-reference compensation resistance from physical500ohm to1kohm gives only modest error improvement and worsens window motion, so it was rejected. Matched reltol-only probe reproduction now supports scoped per-bit attribution; do not prescribe amplifier sizing from peak current alone. Zero-load paired DC reproduces+13.148/-10.478mV offsets. Longer mirror W/L8u/.5u to16u/1u reduces offsets to+8.198/-8.140mV but leaves high-tail compliance deficit; switched-load candidate completed and was rejected: worst reference errors worsened. Wider high input pair and halved high tail multiplicity also remain unadopted; both leave negative tail margin at2.15V. Retained common-mode sweep brackets tail zero margin at1.83\u20131.84V, but error remains15mV at1.8V with positive margin. Compliance alone does not explain static accuracy. High-reference impedance peak39.7ohm and slower bipolar step recovery remain dynamic concerns. Pass473: hybrid high-input stage improves isolated DC/AC/signed steps but actual ADC worst high target error worsens61.35->70.65mV and reference power rises2.05mW; not adopted. Separate static offset from dynamic deviations before selecting another architecture. Completed hybrid outputPMOS-doubled ADC trial reduces worst high-reference target error61.349->56.366mV, but worsens decision-window motion3.179->7.138mV and raises reference power44.423->46.493mW. Event analysis shows stronger recovery during the decision window with similar load charge; candidate remains unadopted. Isolated DC/AC/step improvement does not qualify switched-load regulation. Actual reference demand is bidirectional; sustained reverse-load compliance still fails. Real bias/startup and absolute conversion accuracy remain open.",
